{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789326069,"nonce":"kzxLfVHSjvR7AVSbPkuYjBu3+qc=","title":"Closure call caches miss on every new closure of the same code","message":"Every `Fn.new { }` evaluation allocated a fresh ObjFn as well as the\nObjClosure, in both the interpreter's MakeClosure and the JIT's\nmake_closure helper. The kind-7 call-site cache is keyed by the ObjFn\npointer and the inliner's ClosureFnIs guard compares against it, so a\nclosure created by a later call to the same code never matched: the\nguard failed on every call and the site fell through to the generic\nwren_call path, about 85 ns per call.\n\nReproducer (Mac, tiered llvm, 200k iterations per call, ns per call):\n\n    static adder() { Fn.new {|x| x + 1 } }\n    static wrenClosure(n) { var f = Tally.adder(); var s = 0; for (i in 0...n) s = f.call(s); return s }\n\nbefore: 84-124 (WLIFT_TIER_STATS: call_closure=7.8M, ctx_save_restore=7.8M\nfor 7.8M iterations); the same loop with `f` created once at module\nlevel: 3.7.\n\nFix: one ObjFn per function id, VM::closure_fn, held in VM::closure_fns\nand rooted (with write-back for the moving collector); both closure\ncreation paths share it. After: 3.9 on the short run, 1.1 steady state.\nClosure creation also allocates one object fewer.","files":null}]}